{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant and a small motion plant, then encode the exploration policy in deterministic specifications. Clear sensing leads primarily to random_walk, then a short move_forward pulse, while any obstacle forces a one-shot turn-recovery state. Uncontrollable events are total in every specification state, and action states self-loop on non-critical path_clear so intended pulses are not preempted.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and actuation into plant automata and place policy in specifications",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward coverage with random_walk and short forward pulses, but force obstacle-triggered one-shot turn recovery before returning to exploration",
    "Use direction-consistent recovery: obstacle_left -> clockwise turn, obstacle_right -> counterclockwise turn, obstacle_front -> clockwise turn",
    "Keep full_rotate available only as a dedicated last-resort recovery option, not as the default response"
  ],
